  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Conjecture: Let n be a positive integer, and let G be a group containing no\nelements of order among 2, . . . , n + 1. Then, for any A ⊆ G with |A| = n, we may\nwrite A = {a1 , . . . , an } with a1 , a22 , . . . , ann pairwise distinct.\n   The conjecture is known to hold for n ⩽ 3.                               Z.-W. Sun",
